From 50fdc574baa2d3bfe3ab36be8f6d362441e6cd6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quarx2k <agent00791@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 04:59:27 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Allow atomic replacement of active flowtables

firewall4 reload flushes its rules, deletes the old flowtable and creates
the replacement in one transaction. Ignore flowtables deactivated in the
next generation when checking whether a device hook is already occupied.
Otherwise an existing table makes fw4 check and reload fail with EBUSY.

Use the same generation check as upstream nft_register_flowtable_net_hooks.
Keep rejecting conflicts with flowtables that remain active.

Verified on BE7000 with the signed kmod-nft-core r3 package: boot with both
flow-offload options enabled, repeated fw4 check and actual firewall reload,
switch to software-only offload, and return to PPE/ECM all pass. Hardware
module references remain balanced. No userspace or ABI layout changes.
---
 net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c b/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
index 4eaca57cc..cb318f892 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_tables_api.c
@@ -5905,6 +5905,9 @@ static int nf_tables_newflowtable(struct net *net, struct sock *nlsk,
 			continue;
 
 		list_for_each_entry(ft, &table->flowtables, list) {
+			if (!nft_is_active_next(net, ft))
+				continue;
+
 			for (k = 0; k < ft->ops_len; k++) {
 				if (!ft->ops[k].dev)
 					continue;
